status: 403
request: GET http://www.drugbank.ca/releases/latest/downloads/target-APPROVED-uniprot-links

Probed 2026-09-16 against upstream, without credentials:

  GET /releases/latest/downloads/approved-structure-links
      403  32956 bytes  text/html  (the DrugBank log-in page)
  GET /releases/latest/downloads/APPROVED-structure-links
      403  32956 bytes  text/html  (byte-identical length)
  GET /releases/latest/downloads/target-small_molecule-uniprot-links
      403  32962 bytes  text/html
  GET /releases/latest/downloads/all-drugbank-vocabulary
      403  32954 bytes  text/html

The gate fires before the route resolves, which is why the published slug and
the enum-cased one the client builds are indistinguishable from outside: both
403 with the same page. What a subscriber's request would get for target-APPROVED-uniprot-links is
therefore not a thing this workspace can establish, and the body served here
is synthetic (module docstring, NOTES 5.11). What *is* established is the
gate, and reproducing it is what keeps getInputStream's Base64 Authorization
header load-bearing rather than dead weight.
